    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.33fd651a3723966d655c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Not all proxies can transparently proxy WebSocket connections by default. For example, if you are using Nginx before Grafana you need to configure WebSocket proxy like this:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up Grafana Live",
        "Configure Grafana Live",
        "Request origin check",
        "WebSocket and proxies"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0aa7adff7477bf1c9cc08fa8d9bf3408b5a587b2",
        "sha256": "6a26e75e2110d530ee4277995d1c57bed1fd7312df4d2c2e40d2e5bafd3b9eab",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6e2703b6ba1923a3222",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Some corporate proxies can remove headers required to properly establish a WebSocket connection. In this case, you should tune intermediate proxies to not remove required headers. However, the better option is to use Grafana with TLS. Now WebSocket connection will inherit TLS and thus must be handled transparently by proxies.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up Grafana Live",
        "Configure Grafana Live",
        "Request origin check",
        "WebSocket and proxies"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0aa7adff7477bf1c9cc08fa8d9bf3408b5a587b2",
        "sha256": "6a26e75e2110d530ee4277995d1c57bed1fd7312df4d2c2e40d2e5bafd3b9eab",
        "lineStart": 232,
        "lineEnd": 232,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live.md#L232-L232"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4fa9366fda6a336ca35",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Proxies like Nginx and Envoy have default limits on maximum number of connections which can be established. Make sure you have a reasonable limit for max number of incoming and outgoing connections in your proxy configuration.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up Grafana Live",
        "Configure Grafana Live",
        "Request origin check",
        "WebSocket and proxies"
      ],
      "source": {
