    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cd58056b68cfeb6048d9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also configure a name for the tag. Tag names are useful where the tag has dots in the name and the target data source doesn't allow using dots in labels. For example, you can remap `service.name` to `service_name`. If you don't map any tags here, you can still use any tag in the query, for example: `method=\"${__span.tags.method}\"`. Learn more about [custom query variables](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/tempo/configure-tempo-data-source/#custom-query-variables).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Configure a custom query"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/shared/datasources/tempo-traces-to-profiles.md",
