    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.da7584339129bfe8911d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Soft min** and **soft max** settings can prevent small variations in the data from being magnified when it's mostly flat. In contrast, hard min and max values help prevent obscuring useful detail in the data by clipping intermittent spikes past a specific point.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Placement",
        "Scale",
        "Soft min and soft max"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/shared/visualizations/axis-options-1.md",
