    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c33e78980cebc6a3f46",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In some cases, you might want to display multiple y-axes. For example, if you have a dataset showing both temperature and humidity over time, you might want to show two y-axes with different units for the two series.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Multiple y-axes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/shared/visualizations/multiple-y-axes.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63a62126cad0aebf9166104a4bb5a5f78115a0bf",
        "sha256": "961ba0ec8d94f63b52e439feea0bf5be2095a5939e07dcfcf5d431f1782f5db3",
        "lineStart": 7,
        "lineEnd": 7,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/shared/visualizations/multiple-y-axes.md#L7-L7"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.69438a82109a03d7a90c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can configure multiple y-axes and control where they're displayed in the visualization by adding field overrides. [This example of a dataset that includes temperature and humidity](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/configure-overrides/#example-2-format-temperature-and-humidity) describes how you can configure that. Repeat the steps for every y-axis you wish to display.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Multiple y-axes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/shared/visualizations/multiple-y-axes.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63a62126cad0aebf9166104a4bb5a5f78115a0bf",
        "sha256": "961ba0ec8d94f63b52e439feea0bf5be2095a5939e07dcfcf5d431f1782f5db3",
        "lineStart": 9,
        "lineEnd": 9,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/shared/visualizations/multiple-y-axes.md#L9-L9"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e79181fd488147269b83",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Overrides allow you to customize visualization settings for specific fields or series. When you add an override rule, it targets a particular set of fields and lets you define multiple options for how that field is displayed.",
      "headingPath": [],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/shared/visualizations/overrides-options.md",
