      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you already have Grafana, Loki, or Prometheus running on your system, you might see errors, because the Docker image is trying to use ports that your local installations are already using. If this is the case, stop the services, then run the command again.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Before you begin",
        "Set up the Grafana stack (OSS users)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff2b8ab24871911ae43683a47a84d38a37a462f3",
        "sha256": "50eba38c36063857cdbd025ffdbfc0b905720c10675a0bef69d2878d678b0755",
        "lineStart": 129,
        "lineEnd": 129,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md#L129-L129"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
