    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95460c41c3e46c5919df",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "An [alert instance](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/fundamentals/#alert-instances) is an event that matches a metric returned by an alert rule query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Alert instances"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff2b8ab24871911ae43683a47a84d38a37a462f3",
        "sha256": "50eba38c36063857cdbd025ffdbfc0b905720c10675a0bef69d2878d678b0755",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3425456f234133b40a03",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Let's consider a scenario where you're monitoring website traffic using Grafana. You've set up an alert rule to trigger an alert instance if the number of page views exceeds a certain threshold (more than `1000` page views) within a specific time period, say, over the past `5` minutes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Alert instances"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff2b8ab24871911ae43683a47a84d38a37a462f3",
        "sha256": "50eba38c36063857cdbd025ffdbfc0b905720c10675a0bef69d2878d678b0755",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md#L140-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.32011e0466a103efee43",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If the query returns more than one time-series, each time-series represents a different metric or aspect being monitored. In this case, the alert rule is applied individually to each time-series.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Alert instances"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff2b8ab24871911ae43683a47a84d38a37a462f3",
        "sha256": "50eba38c36063857cdbd025ffdbfc0b905720c10675a0bef69d2878d678b0755",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 142,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md#L142-L142"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
