    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fe43a6a0c6ae24d66b66",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the [life cycle](http://grafana.com/docs/grafana/next/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rule-evaluation/) of alert instances, when an alert condition (threshold) is not met, the alert instance state is **Normal**. Similarly, when the condition is breached (for longer than the pending period, which in this tutorial will be 0), the alert instance state switches back to **Alerting**, which means that the alert rule state is **Firing**, and a notification is sent.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Create an alert rule that returns alert instances",
        "Set evaluation behavior"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt2/index.md",
