    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.04310bf0f194edc63b1b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "These nested policies should route alert instances where the region label is either us-west or us-east. Only the us-west region team should receive grouped alert notifications.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Setting up alert rule grouping",
        "Notification Policy"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt3/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "20141eee062888fed651ddcfe93be449bb31f7fa",
        "sha256": "9d14923e95d9842c88d10c01e4602b74ae99db9107ea2828afb28a7f7a9886e5",
        "lineStart": 268,
        "lineEnd": 268,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt3/index.md#L268-L268"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.91711a095f0c5ab35007",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Label matchers are combined using the `AND` logical operator. This means that all matchers must be satisfied for a rule to be linked to a policy. If you attempt to use the same label key (e.g., region) with different values (e.g., us-west and us-east), the condition will not match, because it is logically impossible for a single key to have multiple values simultaneously.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Setting up alert rule grouping",
        "Notification Policy"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt3/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "20141eee062888fed651ddcfe93be449bb31f7fa",
        "sha256": "9d14923e95d9842c88d10c01e4602b74ae99db9107ea2828afb28a7f7a9886e5",
        "lineStart": 271,
        "lineEnd": 271,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt3/index.md#L271-L271"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5ae1ede51acc54f45737",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "However, `region!=us-east && region=!us-west` can match. For example, it would match a label set where `region=eu-central`. Alternatively, for identical label keys use regular expression matchers (e.g., `region=~us-west|us-east`).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Setting up alert rule grouping",
        "Notification Policy"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt3/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "20141eee062888fed651ddcfe93be449bb31f7fa",
        "sha256": "9d14923e95d9842c88d10c01e4602b74ae99db9107ea2828afb28a7f7a9886e5",
        "lineStart": 273,
