    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.74982130b5adc991c776",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you already have Grafana, Loki, or Prometheus running on your system, you might see errors, because the Docker image is trying to use ports that your local installations are already using. If this is the case, stop the services, then run the command again.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Before you begin",
        "Set up the Grafana stack (OSS users)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 180,
        "lineEnd": 180,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L180-L180"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d722d29b4aef96508682",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana, you can use [templates](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/fundamentals/templates/) to dynamically pull in specific data about the alert rule. This results in more flexible and informative alert notification messages. You can template either alert rule labels and annotations, or notification templates. Both use the Go template language.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 189,
        "lineEnd": 189,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L189-L189"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9bf98a9346d04a595539",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Labels and annotations](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/) are key fields where templates are applied. One of the main advantages of using templating in annotations is the ability to incorporate dynamic data from queries, allowing alerts to reflect real-time information relevant to the triggered condition. By using templating in annotations, you can customize the content of each alert instance, such as including instance names and metric values, so the notification becomes more informative.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works",
        "Templating alert rule labels and annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 195,
        "lineEnd": 195,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L195-L195"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1c8cbf28a252a37c847b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The real power of templating lies in how it helps you format notifications with dynamic alert data. [Notification templates](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/configure-notifications/template-notifications/) let you pull in details from annotations to create clear and consistent messages. They also make it simple to reuse the same format across different contact points, saving time and effort.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works",
        "Notification templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 199,
        "lineEnd": 199,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L199-L199"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.05f1248bb3dd27a24bcb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Notification templates allow you to customize how information is presented in each notification. For example, you can use templates to organize and format details about firing or resolved alerts, making it easier for recipients to understand the status of each alert at a glance—all within a single notification.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works",
        "Notification templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 201,
        "lineEnd": 201,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L201-L201"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e441af801629079bdef4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This particular notification template pulls in summary and description annotations for each alert instance and organizes them into separate sections, such as \"firing\" and \"resolved.\" This way, instead of getting a long list of individual alert notifications, users can receive one well-structured message with all the relevant details grouped together.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works",
        "Notification templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.34e4b8fe008ddced98ff",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This approach is helpful when you want to reduce notification noise, especially in situations where multiple instances of an alert are firing at the same time (e.g., high CPU usage across several instances). You can leverage templates to create a unified, easy-to-read notification that includes all the pertinent details.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "How templating works",
        "Notification templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9f8bbbb902ddfaacbb6d4fc7f0b7f8c161b7d364",
        "sha256": "1fbdb4c76470721474136ce1d34e23afb36bab25b241bf04e5eaeb81091d3737",
        "lineStart": 205,
        "lineEnd": 205,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md#L205-L205"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.62c47842243363d7dc0e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now that we've introduced how templating works, let’s move on to the next step. We guide you through creating an alert rule with a summary and description annotation. In doing so, we incorporate CPU usage and instance names, which we later use in our notification template.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Step 1: Template labels and annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
