    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d862486b306cdaa86707",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now that we’ve configured an alert rule with dynamic templates for the **summary** annotation, the next step is to customize the alert notifications themselves. While the default notification message includes the summary annotation and works well, it can often be too verbose.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Set up the Grafana stack",
        "Step 1: Template labels and annotations",
        "Create an alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt4/index.md",
