    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.39acfba5ed83a8e91e40",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now that the CPU and memory alert rules are set up, they are linked to the notification policies through the custom label matcher we added. The value of the label dynamically changes based on the environment template, using `$labels.instance`. This ensures that the label value will be set to production, staging, or development, depending on the environment.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 3: Create a second alert rule for memory usage"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "576763e1e163885321c5b05f9c62c633240cf1de",
        "sha256": "fb24648fa6bb9daa48fd594a9c0a2392da328eaadefa4de3f494739960a49e51",
        "lineStart": 295,
        "lineEnd": 295,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt5/index.md#L295-L295"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.694eaacaf2ba2afc6abc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Based on your query's `instance` label values (which contain keywords like _prod_ or _staging_ ), Grafana dynamically assigns the value `production`, `staging` or `development` to the custom **environment** label using the template. This dynamic label then matches the label matchers in your notification policies, which route alerts to the correct contact points.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Done! Your alerts are now dynamically routed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "576763e1e163885321c5b05f9c62c633240cf1de",
        "sha256": "fb24648fa6bb9daa48fd594a9c0a2392da328eaadefa4de3f494739960a49e51",
        "lineStart": 302,
        "lineEnd": 302,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt5/index.md#L302-L302"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c761cc697477b4b86a3f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This page shows grouped alerts that are currently triggering notifications. If you click on any alert group to view its label set, contact point, and number of alert instances. Notice that the **environment** label has been dynamically populated with values like `production`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Done! Your alerts are now dynamically routed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt5/index.md",
