        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c3e0ef3f03a38c97ebd3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You'll build a time series visualization to monitor CPU and memory usage, define alert rules with threshold-based conditions, and link those alerts to your dashboards to display real-time annotations when thresholds are breached.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Use case: monitoring and alerting for system health with Prometheus and Grafana",
        "Objective"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
