    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1416ccfa562dafc6d8b3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Try adding a second alert rule using the memory usage metric (`flask_app_memory_usage{instance=\"flask-prod:5000\"`}) to see how combining multiple alerts can enhance your dashboard.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Create an alert rule for CPU usage",
        "Configure notification message"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
        "sha256": "3c3a12e74bf44f9418836365023b811df02411823242ef0b1c737e8697d7bb4c",
        "lineStart": 258,
        "lineEnd": 258,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L258-L258"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6d81aaed1764a138fe99",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "After the alert rules are linked to visualization, they should appear as **health indicators** (colored heart icons: a red heart when the alert is in **Alerting** state, and a green heart when in **Normal** state) on the linked panel. In addition, annotations provide helpful context, such as the time the alert was triggered.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 3: Visualizing metrics and alert annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
        "sha256": "3c3a12e74bf44f9418836365023b811df02411823242ef0b1c737e8697d7bb4c",
        "lineStart": 267,
        "lineEnd": 267,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L267-L267"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dbe474df7e4c9311ac69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Finally, as part of the alerting process, you should receive notifications at the associated contact point. If you're receiving alerts via email, the default email template will include two buttons:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 4: Receiving notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
