    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d7be5727610a53113b29",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **View panel**: links directly to the individual panel where the alert was triggered",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 4: Receiving notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
        "sha256": "3c3a12e74bf44f9418836365023b811df02411823242ef0b1c737e8697d7bb4c",
        "lineStart": 280,
        "lineEnd": 280,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L280-L280"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4f0dc94c175d07eb97d2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, this URL includes `from` and `to` query [parameters](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/configure-notifications/template-notifications/reference/#alert) that reflect the time window around the alert event (one hour before and after the alert). This helps you land directly in the time window where the alert occurred, making it easier to analyze what happened.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 4: Receiving notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
        "sha256": "3c3a12e74bf44f9418836365023b811df02411823242ef0b1c737e8697d7bb4c",
        "lineStart": 286,
        "lineEnd": 286,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L286-L286"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ddabc8429342efac3a35",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you want to define a more intentional time range, you can customize your notifications using a [notification template](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/configure-notifications/template-notifications/examples/#print-a-link-to-a-dashboard-with-time-range). With a template, you can explicitly set `from` and `to` values for more precise control over what users see when they follow the dashboard link. The final URL is constructed using a custom annotation (e.g., `MyDashboardURL`) along with the `from` and `to` parameters, which are calculated in the notification template.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Step 4: Receiving notifications"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
        "sha256": "3c3a12e74bf44f9418836365023b811df02411823242ef0b1c737e8697d7bb4c",
        "lineStart": 288,
        "lineEnd": 288,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md#L288-L288"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss",
          "cloud"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.92c2d662d48391f6f787",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You’ve now linked Prometheus-based alert rules to your Grafana visualizations, giving your dashboards real-time context with alert annotations and health indicators. By visualizing alerts alongside metrics, responders can quickly understand what’s happening and when. You also saw how alert notifications can include direct links to the affected dashboard or panel, helping teams jump straight into the right time window for faster troubleshooting.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/alerting-get-started-pt6/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "edf5e61e1781c10b06ad51461a7e48da7cc824e8",
