    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8450b5e386a4d02b1ad2",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Keep firing for**: defines how long an alert should remain in the Firing state after the alert condition stops being true. During this time, the alert enters a _Recovering_ state, suppressing additional notifications but keeping the alert active. It helps prevent alert flapping, where alerts rapidly switch between firing and resolved due to noisy or unstable metrics.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Before you begin",
        "Create an alert",
        "Set evaluation behavior"
      ],
      "source": {
