    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9226ba46a97193175e22",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Like we did in example 1, let's first mock up our queries. Our query for our vehicle data is very similar to our last query. We use a `from()`, `range()`, and a sequence of `filter()` functions. We then use `AggregateWindow()` and `yield()` to narrow our data even more. In this case, the result is a time series tracking the velocity of our 1983 DeLorean:",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 2: how to create a Grafana alert from two queries and two conditions",
        "Add two Flux queries to your Grafana Alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff67f50b26681d3dc7d4d8e7eb10e4620c9488c3",
        "sha256": "48b344a4b7311941040db4785da4177ce4cd0dcaccadd5ebdd24c843c328bc40",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a91ba6ce24bf21a8b168",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Our second query will trigger an alert whenever our electricity resource (the lightning strike on the Hill Valley clocktower) reaches the needed 1.21 jigowatts. A query like this would look very similar to our vehicle velocity query:",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 2: how to create a Grafana alert from two queries and two conditions",
        "Add two Flux queries to your Grafana Alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff67f50b26681d3dc7d4d8e7eb10e4620c9488c3",
