    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3e8db71fab11632d0bf9",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Now, in section `C` we need to create a math expression to be alerted on. In this case we will use the AND `&&` operator to specify that two conditions must be met: the value of `C` (the reduced value from query `A`) must be greater than 88.0 while the value of `D` (the reduced value from query `B`) must be greater than 1.21. We write this as `$C > 88.0 && $D > 1.21`",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 2: how to create a Grafana alert from two queries and two conditions",
        "Add expressions to your Grafana Alert rule"
      ],
