    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.86f6e12c33db29aa2c58",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this example we showed how to create a Flux-based alert that uses two distinct conditions from two distinct queries that use data from two distinct data sources. For example three we will switch gears and tackle another popular alerting scenario: how to create an alert based on an aggregated (per day) value.",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 2: how to create a Grafana alert from two queries and two conditions",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
