    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf3ce2bc8ebd6d727317",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Let’s assume our electricity meter sends a reading to InfluxDB once per hour and contains the total kWh used for that hour. We want to write a query that will aggregate these per-hour values into a per-day value, then create an alert that triggers when the power consumption (kWh) exceeds 5,000 kWh per day.",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 3: how to create a Grafana Alert based on an aggregated (per-day) value"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md",
