    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f3205a42a7818718f7fc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Plotting and aggregating electrical consumption is a common use case for combining InfluxDB and Grafana. Using Flux, we saw just how easy it can be to group our data by day and then alert on that daily value. In our next two examples we will examine the more complex form of Grafana Alert: multidimensional alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 3: how to create a Grafana Alert based on an aggregated (per-day) value",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
