    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3869f2e7973234a2ad62",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Let’s return to our fluid tanks from example 1, but this time let’s assume we have 5 tanks (A5, B4, C3, D2, and E1). We are now tracking the temperature in five tanks: A5, B4, C3, D2, and E1.",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 4: create a dynamic (multidimensional) Grafana Alert using Flux"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md",
