    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.19715ece44e8fd515a2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Flux queries and Grafana Unified Alerting are a powerful combination to identify practically any alertable conditions in your dataset, or across your entire system. For more information on Grafana Alerting, [visit the documentation here](/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/). For more information on the Flux query language, [you can visit that documentation as well](https://docs.influxdata.com/flux/v0.x/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "How to create Grafana alerts with InfluxDB and the Flux query language",
        "Example 5: how to create a dynamic (multidimensional) Grafana Alert using multiple queries and multiple thresholds with Flux",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff67f50b26681d3dc7d4d8e7eb10e4620c9488c3",
        "sha256": "48b344a4b7311941040db4785da4177ce4cd0dcaccadd5ebdd24c843c328bc40",
        "lineStart": 338,
        "lineEnd": 338,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/create-alerts-from-flux-queries/index.md#L338-L338"
      },
      "applicability": {
