    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c7d213fbdd967054fa25",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "An [alert instance](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/fundamentals/#alert-instances) is a specific occurrence that matches a condition defined by an alert rule, such as when the rate of requests for a specific route suddenly increases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Create a Grafana-managed alert rule"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/grafana-fundamentals/index.md",
