    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.48781fccfbc2c66fd4f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Configuration as code is the practice of storing the configuration of your system as a set of version controlled, human-readable configuration files, rather than in a database. These configuration files can be reused across environments to avoid duplicated resources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Configuration as code"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/provision-dashboards-and-data-sources/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0dfc09eadb6c15b140a27ba0f790c01aebc1bce2",
        "sha256": "6aa77df0c0a5cf00f531e6ad4d5265d2df3b88d40861288670242302195edb66",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/tutorials/provision-dashboards-and-data-sources/index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8bbdfaf563c38383efbd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As the number of dashboards and data sources grows within your organization, manually managing changes can become tedious and error-prone. Encouraging reuse becomes important to avoid multiple teams redesigning the same dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Configuration as code"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/tutorials/provision-dashboards-and-data-sources/index.md",
