    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fc2a94a683284211d92d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Previously, if no organization role mapping was found for a user when they connected using OAuth, Grafana didn't update the user’s organization role.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.1",
        "Technical notes",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3b1ecb3d17de83a0ecf8b3d3d021441e75a512b9",
        "sha256": "249f6ba45dce92e805e500828d4076f1731835584ab1a1e7e63459ec1042873a",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md#L27-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8a06722798695f43e8bd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Grafana 10.1, on every login, if the `role_attribute_path` property doesn't return a role, then the user is assigned the role specified by the `auto_assign_org_role` option or the default role for the organization, which is Viewer by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.1",
        "Technical notes",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3b1ecb3d17de83a0ecf8b3d3d021441e75a512b9",
        "sha256": "249f6ba45dce92e805e500828d4076f1731835584ab1a1e7e63459ec1042873a",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f9edf285fed9ab2d4807",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To avoid overriding manually set roles, enable the `skip_org_role_sync` option in the Grafana configuration for your OAuth provider before upgrading to Grafana 10.1 and before users log in for the first time on Grafana 10.1.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.1",
        "Technical notes",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3b1ecb3d17de83a0ecf8b3d3d021441e75a512b9",
        "sha256": "249f6ba45dce92e805e500828d4076f1731835584ab1a1e7e63459ec1042873a",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.1/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.511b85a73b7ce99284fc",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- From Grafana v10.2 onwards, `/api/datasources/:id/` is removed and replaced with `/api/access-control/datasources/:uid`. For more information about the new API endpoints for the data source permission API, refer to the [documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/developers/http_api/datasource_permissions/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.2",
        "Technical notes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "649c8cc58b542d7d898594ef6c5987d085d82e51",
        "sha256": "72f1508658a101ee2dddb26c3211d2f86d1c60d5695b907becc5f7113dcb8e23",
        "lineStart": 23,
        "lineEnd": 23,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.2/index.md#L23-L23"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3558dd992d72628fec37",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you haven't already upgraded to Grafana Alerting from legacy Alerting, Grafana will initiate a dry-run of the upgrade every time the instance starts. This is in preparation for the removal of legacy Alerting in Grafana v11. The dry-run logs the results of the upgrade attempt and identifies any issues requiring attention before you can successfully execute the upgrade. No changes are made during the dry-run.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.4",
        "Technical notes",
        "Legacy alerting -> Grafana Alerting dry-run on start"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9969ccc7cfcb74d5335f6722dfbb31edaee14d07",
        "sha256": "6ae44c99b4628734b89f13613439313a828ef9b96f14dc1e899c4d8531a17e97",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1eb2925f9cc4633fa08e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can disable this behavior using the feature flag `alertingUpgradeDryrunOnStart`:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.4",
        "Technical notes",
        "Legacy alerting -> Grafana Alerting dry-run on start"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9969ccc7cfcb74d5335f6722dfbb31edaee14d07",
        "sha256": "6ae44c99b4628734b89f13613439313a828ef9b96f14dc1e899c4d8531a17e97",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.00c70582fe1dfd187a1f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We strongly encourage you to review the [upgrade guide](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/v10.4/alerting/set-up/migrating-alerts/) and perform the necessary upgrade steps prior to v11.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v10.4",
        "Technical notes",
        "Legacy alerting -> Grafana Alerting dry-run on start"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9969ccc7cfcb74d5335f6722dfbb31edaee14d07",
        "sha256": "6ae44c99b4628734b89f13613439313a828ef9b96f14dc1e899c4d8531a17e97",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 36,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v10.4/index.md#L36-L36"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d3c87212c9ad63fbdbde",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've had a standard ways to define UIDs for Grafana objects for years (at least [since Grafana v5](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/7883)). While all of our internal code complies to this format, we didn't yet have strict enforcement of this format in REST APIs and provisioning paths that allow the creation and update of data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v11.2",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana data source UID format enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v11.2/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d8e161897dc9ede0bafb5626643eacd93c9f2716",
        "sha256": "5213761bddcf0b2d7f0d4257af140f7f9b6fbc232b3b01aab260f9a53ae9bc0c",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v11.2/index.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cd643a362ba9acfad298",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana v11.2, we [added](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/89363/files) a new feature flag called `failWrongDSUID` that is turned off by default. When enabled, the REST APIs and provisioning start rejecting any requests to create or update data source instances that have an incorrect UID.",
      "headingPath": [
