    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.19f94b542826c153e70c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've had standard ways to define UIDs for Grafana objects for years (at least [since Grafana v5](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/7883)). While all of our internal code complies with this format, we haven't strictly enforced this format in REST APIs and provisioning paths that allow the creation and update of data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v12.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana data source UID format enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v12.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b166cc2c022b2c90b4b8cf4b799f14f35b8d3f8a",
        "sha256": "a2a5393118afe370366dedd39dd09bc3d241107f8a440b67a2541b4c0bdbe544",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v12.0/index.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d390f0bceb7596c1051",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana v11.2, we [added](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/89363/files) a new feature flag called `failWrongDSUID` that is turned off by default. When enabled, the REST APIs and provisioning reject any requests to create or update data source instances that have an incorrect UID.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v12.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana data source UID format enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v12.0/index.md",
