      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a63d82231c0a1280712c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana now requires all plugins to be signed. If a plugin is not signed Grafana will not load/start it. This is an additional security measure to make sure plugin files and binaries haven't been tampered with. All Grafana Labs authored plugins, including Enterprise plugins, are now signed. It's possible to allow unsigned plugins using a configuration setting, but is something we strongly advise against doing. For more information about this setting, refer to [allow loading unsigned plugins](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#allow_loading_unsigned_plugins).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.25093fb5fd960bc25e0b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When WebSocket connection is established, Grafana checks the request Origin header due to security reasons (for example, to prevent hijacking of WebSocket connection). If you have a properly defined public URL (`root_url` server option) then the origin check should successfully pass for WebSocket requests originating from public URL pages. In case of an unsuccessful origin check, Grafana returns a 403 error. It's also possible to add a list of additional origin patterns for the origin check.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana Live"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8b1c2db646a4b747f3c7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To handle many concurrent WebSocket connections you may need to tune your OS settings or infrastructure. Grafana Live is enabled by default and supports 100 concurrent WebSocket connections max to avoid possible problems with the file descriptor OS limit. As soon as your setup meets the requirements to scale the number of persistent connections this limit can be increased. You also have an option to disable Grafana Live.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana Live"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.714f5cebd33d996d244d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Refer to [Grafana Live configuration](../../setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live/) documentation for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Grafana Live"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 41,
        "lineEnd": 41,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L41-L41"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9bafba985541c92fb241",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana v8.0 changes the underlying data structure to [data frames](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/data-frames) for the Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources. As a result, a _Time series_ query result gets returned in a [wide format](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/data-frames#wide-format). To make the visualizations work as they did before, you might have to do some manual migrations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c8bffb70913e5ad683e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For any existing panels/visualizations using a _Time series_ query, where the time column is only needed for filtering the time range, for example, using the bar gauge or pie chart panel, we recommend that you use a _Table query_ instead and exclude the time column as a field in the response. Refer to this [issue comment](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/35534#issuecomment-861519658) for detailed instructions and workarounds.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L47-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1b0e3e283266ec2f74e4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you have a query where there's a time value and a numeric value selected together with a string value that's not named _metric_, the graph panel renders series names as `value <hostname>` rather than just `<hostname>` which was the case before Grafana 8.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources",
        "Prefix added to series names"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.393cb0d4ad6f4c8f381e",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. In Grafana v8.0.3, use an alias of the string column selected as `metric`. for example, `hostname as metric`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources",
        "Prefix added to series names"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.37cfb8f41bf6964fb6ee",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "2. Use the [Standard field definitions' display name](../../panels-visualizations/configure-standard-options/#display-name) to format the alias. For the preceding example query, you would use `${__field.labels.hostname}` option.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources",
        "Prefix added to series names"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 68,
        "lineEnd": 68,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L68-L68"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6d9dd552bec8e8f93dbd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information, refer to the our relational databases documentation of [Postgres](../../datasources/postgres/#time-series-queries), [MySQL](../../datasources/mysql/#time-series-queries), [Microsoft SQL Server](../../datasources/mssql/query-editor/#time-series-query-examples).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Postgres, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server data sources",
        "Prefix added to series names"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "720c71960c241f7ae31c7589d8ab8c0e9e415c15",
        "sha256": "ca385af51b86ede32f03420fc5395bf582b30cc7f433e0f12b358b8c96f64653",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.0/index.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1832ba045e068c36cef5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As of Grafana v8.1, we no longer support unencrypted storage of passwords and basic auth passwords.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.1",
        "Technical notes",
        "Use of unencrypted passwords for data sources no longer supported"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.1/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "17e06c6365752c282876de9d9fb5e53afea6e129",
        "sha256": "96a2884a1d399d791a1fcd96867099f3070403250e253f49074d728320535dfa",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.1/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0dff95f2c8df9ffc5c64",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To migrate to encrypted storage, use a `grafana-cli` command to migrate all of your data sources to use encrypted storage of secrets. See [migrate data and encrypt passwords](../../cli/#migrate-data-and-encrypt-passwords) for further instructions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.1",
        "Technical notes",
        "Use of unencrypted passwords for data sources no longer supported"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.1/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "17e06c6365752c282876de9d9fb5e53afea6e129",
        "sha256": "96a2884a1d399d791a1fcd96867099f3070403250e253f49074d728320535dfa",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.1/index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf328771bf6d3ebbbadc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In 8.3, Grafana dashboards now reference data sources using an object with `uid` and `type` properties instead of the data source name property. A schema migration is applied when existing dashboards open. If you provision dashboards to multiple Grafana instances, then we recommend that you also provision data sources. You can specify the `uid` to be the same for data sources across your instances. If you need to find the `uid` for a data source created in the UI, check the URL of the data source settings page. The URL follows the pattern ` /data source/edit/${uid}`, meaning the last part is the `uid`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.3",
        "Technical notes",
        "Dashboard references"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.3/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "be39a1eb3dc7370ed841bd3584f646504abe712e",
        "sha256": "a55090dd81d342a481a9af6eeee20df2e655f7495aac7bf2f15f1581196965ce",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 32,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.3/index.md#L31-L32"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf312f7a00c9b7d26aae",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The concept of a `default` data source existed in Grafana since the beginning. However, the meaning and behavior were not clear. The default data source was not just the starting data source for new panels but it was also saved using a special value (null). This made it possible to change the default data source to another and have that change impact all dashboards that used the default data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.5",
        "Technical notes",
        "Default data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2c0a3d63cb408359f6c1ae192bc192b5990b2ec0",
        "sha256": "32e03b3fce31e49f7764e85dd82c6ed7acdb4f4fb8f029e9ee32857c46b4d4d5",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.5/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.93d59ad451a35d78ae19",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This behavior was not very intuitive and creates issues for users who want to change the default without it impacting existing dashboards. That is why we are changing the behavior in 8.5. From now on, the `default` data source will not be a persisted property but just the starting data source for new panels and queries. Existing dashboards that still have panels with a `datasource` set to null will be migrated when the dashboard opens. The migration will set the data source property to the **current** default data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v8.5",
        "Technical notes",
        "Default data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "2c0a3d63cb408359f6c1ae192bc192b5990b2ec0",
        "sha256": "32e03b3fce31e49f7764e85dd82c6ed7acdb4f4fb8f029e9ee32857c46b4d4d5",
        "lineStart": 33,
        "lineEnd": 35,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v8.5/index.md#L33-L35"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e91b9f34d2f1de1646b3",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Built-in roles are now called basic roles. They now consist of permissions, not roles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Role-based access control: changes for general release"
      ],
      "source": {
