      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1e690d2da1b67428a15b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Therefore, any secret created or updated in Grafana v9.0 won't be decryptable by any previous Grafana version unless the feature toggle `envelopeEncryption` is enabled in the previous version (only available since v8.3). This needs to be considered in high availability setups, progressive rollouts or in case of need to roll back to a previous Grafana version for any reason.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L85-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "conditional-or-paid-restriction-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4896da6aeec725796ae4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The recommendation here is to enable `envelopeEncryption` for older versions, or alternatively enable `disableEnvelopeEncryption` before upgrading to v9.0. However, the latter is probably going to be removed in one of the next releases, so we hugely encourage to move on with envelope encryption.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 89,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L89-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf32f37a965e71cf5b84",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Find [here](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/configure-database-encryption/) more details and some possible workarounds in case you end up in an undesired situation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L93-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6439473a5b172343a853",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When we release Grafana 9.0 on June 14th, Grafana will no longer enforce viewers and editor-admins differently. That means that regardless of whether your Grafana Enterprise license is tiered or combined, instead of seeing this on the Stats & Licensing page:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 98,
        "lineEnd": 98,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L98-L98"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0 > Technical notes > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e42b083da898033c04e3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It also means that Grafana will count all users the same, regardless of their role, including org roles (Viewer, Editor, Admin) and fine-grained roles (Dashboard Editor, Reports Editor, etc.). You won’t see a separate warning banner or see users locked out if you hit your limit of viewers or editor-admins, only your total combined limit of active users.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0 > Technical notes > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c5ad0d3591adba5b53de",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you have a license for 10 active admins and 100 active viewers in your Grafana Enterprise license, then starting in v9.0 you will have a limit of 110 active users, and it doesn’t matter what roles those users have, they will all be counted and enforced the same.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0",
        "Technical notes",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9c75c1b4710425fed311d0b9c4aad9bcfc19f3b3",
        "sha256": "5fb0e39fcd09f568768db47399fc898425a0bb376bc3ad5c91bc9d11a4c1fe4d",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 108,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.0/index.md#L108-L108"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "Upgrade to Grafana v9.0 > Technical notes > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.314930f7f92f44c24fcc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The upgrade to Grafana v9.4 includes changes to the Grafana database for Grafana alerting that are not backward compatible. As a result, when you upgrade to Grafana v9.4, do not downgrade your Grafana instance to an earlier version. Doing so might cause issues with managing your Grafana alerts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.4",
        "Technical notes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.4/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "61df0bb6528c849873259336765b6ec9be6901e8",
        "sha256": "07814b81a11a3d4e1db5fb57b517ecc737040bb7afe5bc20e58e10334eaa55b7",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.4/index.md#L27-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf9a381f3e519384e50f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Beginning in v9.5, the InfluxDB data source deprecates the `database` field in provisioning files. The `dbName` field under `jsonData` must be used to store the database information. For more information and examples, please refer to [InfluxDB Provisioning](../../datasources/influxdb/#provision-the-data-source).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.5",
        "Technical notes",
        "InfluxDB provisioning change"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "26dc25a4f9e3008d0b2c3b5b71b8d9b43b24ed91",
        "sha256": "dc3cbc0fd3bd18f39ec4457795f8ef9e6d4a1ee1e2440b169405dec5f0fd2437",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md#L29-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8a48cfdfc01584ee952b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We are deprecating the dashboard previews feature and will remove it in Grafana v10. We've started exploring alternative ways of adding visual previews using the Scenes framework, and we'll share more information about it in the future.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.5",
        "Technical notes",
        "Dashboard previews deprecation notice"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "26dc25a4f9e3008d0b2c3b5b71b8d9b43b24ed91",
        "sha256": "dc3cbc0fd3bd18f39ec4457795f8ef9e6d4a1ee1e2440b169405dec5f0fd2437",
        "lineStart": 35,
        "lineEnd": 35,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md#L35-L35"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.68674f1a08100f773590",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We are upgrading Grafana [API keys](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/service-accounts/migrate-api-keys/) to service accounts. Service accounts are a superset of API keys that include token rotation and compatibility with [Role-based access control](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/). In a future release, we'll automatically migrate all existing API keys to service accounts. All of your existing tokens will continue to work; they will simply be migrated to service accounts. You can preempt this change by migrating your existing API keys to service accounts using Grafana's UI or API. Learn how to do this in the [API keys documentation](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/service-accounts/migrate-api-keys/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Upgrade to Grafana v9.5",
        "Technical notes",
        "Migrate your API keys to service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "26dc25a4f9e3008d0b2c3b5b71b8d9b43b24ed91",
        "sha256": "dc3cbc0fd3bd18f39ec4457795f8ef9e6d4a1ee1e2440b169405dec5f0fd2437",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v9.5/index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c718eb40b44481fbb58",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Having a dependable release process provides users like you with the best Grafana experience possible, and it provides the flexibility to upgrade in a manner that works best for you and your organization.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 19,
        "lineEnd": 19,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L19-L19"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5c8e39903349ea4bc042",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Minor release (every other month)**: These releases can include new features, deprecation notices, notices about upcoming breaking changes, previously announced breaking changes, bug fixes, and security vulnerability patches.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "What to expect from each release type"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.603e32184a48f440484f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Major release (once a year, in April/May)**: These are like a minor release, but accompanied by [GrafanaCON](https://grafana.com/events/grafanacon/) and a comprehensive upgrade guide for users who like to upgrade only once a year.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "What to expect from each release type"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 30,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L30-L30"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ab19c58920a460051e82",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Patching release (at least every month)**: These include bug fixes for currently supported versions, as well as any security vulnerability patches.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "What to expect from each release type"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d4cf135ad9eda89a04d4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can choose your cadence: For frequent self-managed updates, you should follow the minor release (for example, upgrade 11.1 to 11.2), which also gives you access to the latest features. If you need a longer period to review our new releases, you should follow the major releases. Both strategies get patching releases with security fixes (high severity security fixes also result in ad-hoc patch releases). We’ll get into additional guidance on upgrade cadences later in this guide.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "What to expect from each release type"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 33,
        "lineEnd": 33,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L33-L33"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.807ec2715a431e963c24",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We love sharing all our great features with you so you can leverage Grafana to its fullest. We also understand that complete release documentation allows you to upgrade with confidence. Whether it’s knowing that a bug has been fixed, seeing that a security vulnerability is patched, or understanding how to mitigate the impact of breaking changes, proper documentation allows you to make informed decisions about when to upgrade your local Grafana instances.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "How to find the specifics for a release"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 38,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L37-L38"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b1b180ab3e3b25f8ef3f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We provide release documentation in multiple places to address different needs:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "How to find the specifics for a release"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
