    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.75d0085831d319ae3781",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Release freezes: Each year Grafana implements two release freezes to accommodate for the holiday season. During these times, no scheduled releases will be executed. However, this does not apply to changes that may be required during the course of an operational or security incident.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "When to expect releases",
        "A few important notes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3ded8bc07e417cd83716",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the past, critical vulnerabilities triggered unscheduled releases that incremented the patch version (e.g., 10.3.0 to 10.3.1). However, we found that the naming convention for these releases didn't clearly communicate the nature of the update. For example, if there was a version change from 11.3.0 to 11.3.1, there was no indication whether it was a security fix, a bug fix, or a minor feature update. This lack of clarity led to confusion about the urgency and nature of the update. <br>",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Grafana security releases: improved version naming convention"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4d758cf0cf07c2030c3f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Docker does not allow the plus sign (`+`) in image tag names. A plus sign (`+`) will be a rendered as a dash (`-`) in the docker tag.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Grafana security releases: improved version naming convention"
      ],
      "source": {
