        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1f01f6e42e999d26935e",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "2. We perform manual acceptance and smoke testing internally for new features by deploying to our internal observability stack. After that, we progressively roll out in Grafana Cloud, and then cut an OSS and Enterprise release. Each stage catches bugs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "How the Grafana team catches bugs and breaks during the release process"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 173,
        "lineEnd": 173,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L173-L173"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.806e3463d4e0b98c5e1e",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "3. We ship new features in Experimental or Private Preview [release stages](https://grafana.com/docs/release-life-cycle/), behind feature toggles. This helps us improve the feature during development. If you are interested in gaining early access to features (including in your development or test environments), please let us know.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "How the Grafana team catches bugs and breaks during the release process"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 174,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L174-L174"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a63437f9622df520439",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "4. We scan Grafana, all plugins and their dependencies continuously for security vulnerabilities.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "How the Grafana team catches bugs and breaks during the release process"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 175,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L175-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
