    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ebcff6b63df4c477d448",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Despite thorough testing, you can experience problems when upgrading:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Minimize the likelihood of bugs and problems during upgrade"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 179,
        "lineEnd": 179,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L179-L179"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3976289b3bbcac0eb08d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Bugs are unexpected side effects of code changes in the release, which cause problems. Some bugs occur for all users, and we usually catch these in the early stages of testing. Others occur in a small number of Grafana instances with specific configuration or unusual use cases; for example a specific authentication setup or a combination of feature toggles. Grafana plugins also interact with external services via API to query data, and sometimes these APIs change without notice, causing issues for your dashboards that depend on these datasources. Grafana Labs has monitoring in place to regularly test these APIs, but at times they break in unexpected ways.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Minimize the likelihood of bugs and problems during upgrade",
        "Bugs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 183,
        "lineEnd": 183,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L183-L183"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d55cd0c28ffcd1e80326",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Reduce the risk of bugs by staying current and rolling out upgrades across dev or test environments before production. A Grafana Enterprise license entitles you to an additional dev and test instance for this purpose, available through your account team, and in Grafana Cloud you can create dev and test stacks that upgrade before production by using [rolling release channels](https://grafana.com/docs/rolling-release/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Minimize the likelihood of bugs and problems during upgrade",
        "Bugs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 185,
        "lineEnd": 185,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L185-L185"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2d96fb518456165005bb",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Back up your database on a regular basis, and especially before you upgrade.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Minimize the likelihood of bugs and problems during upgrade",
        "Bugs"
      ],
      "source": {
