    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.aaf64ed86b9deb720a5b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana core** ships as a single binary and consists of Dashboards, Alerts, Explore, Authentication and Authorization, Reporting, some core data sources, and other components. However, almost everyone who uses Grafana also uses **plugins**: panels, data sources, and applications that are released independently of Grafana. Every plugin version lists its Grafana version dependencies (you can see them at [https://grafana.com/grafana/plugins/](https://grafana.com/grafana/plugins/)) but different versions of different plugins can also interact with each other - for example you might visualize data from a data source in a panel in Grafana, all three of which are versioned independently of each other. That can create issues that are hard to catch in testing.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Strategies for upgrading your self-managed Grafana instance",
        "Minimize the likelihood of bugs and problems during upgrade",
        "Plugin incompatibility"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4d2b4a87fa81e54c20f7dba4437026da8cd92d2d",
        "sha256": "3f9a1a0855780d964fc5f80e1f788ab4e9ab47a0c898a30be3c86224faeb133a",
        "lineStart": 199,
        "lineEnd": 199,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/upgrade-guide/when-to-upgrade/index.md#L199-L199"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d204b2432957b2fa29fd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A Grafana dashboard is a set of one or more panels that provide an at-a-glance view of related information. These panels are the basic building block in Grafana dashboards, and they're created using components that query and transform raw data from a data source into charts, graphs, and other visualizations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b05e1bba167c2f9996b1300ba8d97d2218c4f4b",
        "sha256": "008b50287749306da921dbb975fb8fff9a53fc2bf7241cd5294d0ddaad37c115",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.415c5a3ed0ff483720ef",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A data source can be an SQL database, Grafana Loki, Grafana Mimir, or a JSON-based API. It can even be a basic CSV file. Queries allow you to reduce the entirety of your data to a specific dataset, providing a more manageable visualization. Data source plugins take a query you want answered, retrieve the data from the data source, and reconcile the differences between the data model of the data source and the data model of Grafana dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b05e1bba167c2f9996b1300ba8d97d2218c4f4b",
        "sha256": "008b50287749306da921dbb975fb8fff9a53fc2bf7241cd5294d0ddaad37c115",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c70602c7993e487d4c6b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The growing suite of Grafana visualizations, ranging from time series graphs to heatmaps to cutting-edge 3D charts, provide you several different ways to present your data within a panel, depending on what best suits the data and your needs. If the data format in a visualization doesn’t meet your requirements, you can apply a transformation that manipulates the data returned by a query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b05e1bba167c2f9996b1300ba8d97d2218c4f4b",
        "sha256": "008b50287749306da921dbb975fb8fff9a53fc2bf7241cd5294d0ddaad37c115",
        "lineStart": 41,
        "lineEnd": 41,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md#L41-L41"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e41eb889c6fdb5df1e06",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With 150+ data source plugins, you can unify all your data sources into a single dashboard to streamline data monitoring and troubleshooting. With Grafana, you can translate, transform, and visualize data in flexible and versatile dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0b05e1bba167c2f9996b1300ba8d97d2218c4f4b",
        "sha256": "008b50287749306da921dbb975fb8fff9a53fc2bf7241cd5294d0ddaad37c115",
        "lineStart": 43,
        "lineEnd": 43,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/_index.md#L43-L43"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6f3ae3723b4ab86af832",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A Grafana dashboard is a set of one or more [panels](ref:panels), organized and arranged into one or more rows or tabs, that provide an at-a-glance view of related information. These panels are created using components that query and transform raw data from a data source into visualizations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "84c4663f904afd41ead2058371d4a2edf4b22cf6",
        "sha256": "137255711befaf144a2a312db898acc25d71d0e198dc4173513bad4b5ee82558",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.92880ede06cef0f73c9c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A data source can be an SQL database, Grafana Loki, Grafana Mimir, or an API endpoint. It can even be a basic CSV file. Data source plugins take a query you want answered, retrieve the data from the data source, and reconcile the differences between the data model of the data source and the data model of Grafana dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "84c4663f904afd41ead2058371d4a2edf4b22cf6",
        "sha256": "137255711befaf144a2a312db898acc25d71d0e198dc4173513bad4b5ee82558",
        "lineStart": 66,
        "lineEnd": 66,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md#L66-L66"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.898ee48e803d930a033f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Queries allow you to reduce the entirety of your data to a specific dataset, providing a more manageable visualization. Since data sources have their own distinct query languages, Grafana dashboards provide you with a query editor to accommodate these differences.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "84c4663f904afd41ead2058371d4a2edf4b22cf6",
        "sha256": "137255711befaf144a2a312db898acc25d71d0e198dc4173513bad4b5ee82558",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5bce5da4115fffd523dc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A panel is the container that displays the visualization and provides you with various controls to manipulate it. Panel options let you customize many aspects of a visualization and the options differ based on which visualization you select. When the data format in a visualization doesn't meet your requirements, you can apply a transformation that manipulates the data returned by a query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "84c4663f904afd41ead2058371d4a2edf4b22cf6",
        "sha256": "137255711befaf144a2a312db898acc25d71d0e198dc4173513bad4b5ee82558",
        "lineStart": 72,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/_index.md#L72-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
