    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.45a7620425344d711572",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Query variables enable you to write a data source query that can return a list of metric names, tag values, or keys. For example, a query variable might return a list of server names, sensor IDs, or data centers. The variable values change as they dynamically fetch options with a data source query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 132,
        "lineEnd": 132,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L132-L132"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.66d94218a26b4f5ecfa8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Query variables are generally only supported for strings. If your query returns numbers or any other data type, you might need to convert them to strings to use them as variables. For the Azure data source, for example, you can use the [`tostring`](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-explorer/kusto/query/tostringfunction) function for this purpose.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c84f0ec3ebddbc715013",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Query expressions can contain references to other variables and in effect create linked variables. Grafana detects this and automatically refreshes a variable when one of its linked variables change.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a query variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
