    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.42e285e765089d9bb369",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "_Constant_ variables enable you to define a hidden constant. This is useful for metric path prefixes for dashboards you want to share. When you export a dashboard, constant variables are converted to import options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a constant variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 234,
        "lineEnd": 234,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L234-L234"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.81fa0c1ee2df47de12f1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Constant variables are _not_ flexible. Each constant variable only holds one value, and it cannot be updated unless you update the variable settings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a constant variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 236,
        "lineEnd": 236,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L236-L236"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f010fa531a312e7d9496",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Constant variables are useful when you have complex values that you need to include in queries but don't want to retype in every query. For example, if you had a server path called `i-0b6a61efe2ab843gg`, then you could replace it with a variable called `$path_gg`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add a constant variable"
      ],
      "source": {
