    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ede832c95f1d7386940a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use an _interval_ variable to represents time spans such as `1m`,`1h`, `1d`. You can think of them as a dashboard-wide \"group by time\" command. Interval variables change how the data is grouped in the visualization. You can also use the Auto Option to return a set number of data points per time span.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add an interval variable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 269,
        "lineEnd": 269,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L269-L269"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7a95d2aab4749aa63b4c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use an interval variable as a parameter to group by time (for InfluxDB), date histogram interval (for Elasticsearch), or as a summarize function parameter (for Graphite).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Add an interval variable"
      ],
      "source": {
