    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8781ab48af1b93476ae1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Selection Options** are a feature you can use to manage variable option selections for query and custom variables. All selection options are optional, and they're off by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 348,
        "lineEnd": 348,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L348-L348"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7ead237e2b9c865fe9b5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Interpolating a variable with multiple values selected is tricky as it's not straight forward how to format the multiple values into a string that's valid in the given context where the variable is used. Grafana tries to solve this by allowing each data source plugin to inform the templating interpolation engine what format to use for multiple values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 352,
        "lineEnd": 352,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L352-L352"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8d4a42616785f2c8b0da",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The **Custom all value** option on the variable must be blank for Grafana to format all values into a single string. If it's left blank, then Grafana concatenates (adds together) all the values in the query. Something like `value1,value2,value3`. If a custom `all` value is used, then instead the value is something like `*` or `all`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 355,
        "lineEnd": 355,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L355-L355"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a571d5922c29910f377a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Graphite uses glob expressions. A variable with multiple values would, in this case, be interpolated as `{host1,host2,host3}` if the current variable value was _host1_, _host2_, and _host3_.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Multi-value variables with a Graphite data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 360,
        "lineEnd": 360,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L360-L360"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3e3d59ead7f00950aa65",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "InfluxDB and Prometheus use regular expressions, so the same variable would be interpolated as `(host1|host2|host3)`. Every value would also be regular expression escaped. If not, a value with a regular expression control character would break the regular expression.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Multi-value variables with a Prometheus or InfluxDB data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 364,
        "lineEnd": 364,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L364-L364"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a294d032fa3b45b8001",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Elasticsearch uses Lucene query syntax, so the same variable would be formatted as `(\"host1\" OR \"host2\" OR \"host3\")`. In this case, every value must be escaped so that the value only contains Lucene control words and quotation marks.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Multi-value variables with an Elastic data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 368,
        "lineEnd": 368,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L368-L368"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3b972c5602c6ae026e15",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you have a multi-value variable that's formatted as an array, you can use array positions to reference the values rather than the actual values. You can use this functionality in dashboard panels to filter data, and when you do so, the array is maintained.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Variable indexing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 372,
        "lineEnd": 373,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L372-L373"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.432c1e651492810c03b7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To reference variable values this way, use the following syntax:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Variable indexing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 375,
        "lineEnd": 375,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L375-L375"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1a4b27f3b61aa75e523e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the following example, there's an array of three values, `1t`, `2t`, and `3t`, and rather than referencing those values, the panel query references the second value in the array using the syntax `${query0.1}`:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Variable indexing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 383,
        "lineEnd": 383,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L383-L383"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f6a0fbbe325ec8d6790b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Automatic escaping and formatting can cause problems and it can be tricky to grasp the logic behind it. Especially for InfluxDB and Prometheus where the use of regular expression syntax requires that the variable is used in regular expression operator context.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Troubleshoot multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 389,
        "lineEnd": 389,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L389-L389"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0eab65a2914409e78858",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you don't want Grafana to do this automatic regular expression escaping and formatting, then you must do one of the following:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
        "Variable selection options",
        "Multi-value variables",
        "Troubleshoot multi-value variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4457b936a9bfd014008fb8f048e6298c3d09adf4",
        "sha256": "4974eb465335c4f545040002170c2cbf56fce6881ca54c1b130c25cf2a89ca17",
        "lineStart": 391,
        "lineEnd": 391,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/add-template-variables.md#L391-L391"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.237eed5b39996471554b",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Turn off the **Multi-value** or **Include All option** options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Add variables",
