    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.157f35357b82ac3056eb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To create a custom variable with multiple properties, define a JSON array, like this:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Multi-property variables",
        "Multi-property custom variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.828857961204cd0d8e46",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Then you can use `${varName.someProperty}` syntax to reference any property in your dashboard panels or metrics:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Multi-property variables",
        "Multi-property custom variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.27faf424efe87f9ddf23",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can even deeply nest properties and still access them using familiar variable syntax. In the following example, each user has an address property with all the elements of an address nested within it:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Multi-property variables",
        "Multi-property custom variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 69,
        "lineEnd": 69,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L69-L69"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ed6f677abca2118b1639",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Because query configuration is different for each data source, there's no one way to set up a JSON array to create a multi-property query variable. For PostgreSQL, refer to [PostgreSQL template variables](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/postgres/template-variables/). For other data sources, refer to the relevant [Data sources documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/datasources/) for preinstalled data source plugins. For configuration information on all other data source plugins, refer to the [Plugins documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/plugins/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Multi-property variables",
        "Multi-property query variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L75-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a19a6d51eb8bb4820fd7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "_Chained variables_, also called _linked variables_ or _nested variables_, are query variables with one or more other variables in their variable query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 82,
        "lineEnd": 82,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L82-L82"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ae04dcc0e9be442d1147",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Chained variables create dependent relationships where the options available in one variable depend on the selections made in another. This pattern enables cascading filters that help users drill down through hierarchical data structures.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L84-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c7046d86e5b5d6a5dcb6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Technically, there is no limit to how many variables you can chain together, but the more links you have, the greater the query load.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
        "lineStart": 90,
        "lineEnd": 90,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md#L90-L90"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.65c57bca74014eddf8f7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The following Grafana Play dashboards contain basic chained variables, only two layers deep. To view the variables and their settings, click **Edit** in the top-right corner of the dashboard, click the **Dashboard options** icon in the toolbar, and expand the **Variables** section. Both examples are expanded in the following section.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables",
        "Grafana Play dashboard examples"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "415fc951b326f41b7cb50b9b9eed4c53a5c88dc1",
        "sha256": "da9a7965e6d76b0630a4522a27d8b6bd55d3fa7bda11f49a6c6214da65f8ff20",
