    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.252dc9e610aa2a1f744f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, you could make separate variables for each metric source, but then you have to know which server goes with which app. A better solution is to use one variable to filter another. In this example, when the user changes the value of the `app` variable, it changes the drop-down options returned by the `server` variable. Both variables use the **Multi-value** option and **Include all option**, enabling users to select some or all options presented at any time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables",
        "Grafana Play dashboard examples",
        "Graphite example explained"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/advanced-variables.md",
