    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e785cc49188777629664",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- The easiest way to create a new chained variable is to copy the variable that you want to base the new one on. In the variable list, click the **Duplicate variable** icon to the right of the variable entry to create a copy. You can then add on to the query for the parent variable.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Advanced variable configurations",
        "Chained variables",
        "Best practices for chained variables",
        "New linked variables creation"
      ],
