    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f881c497db1d52812c8f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use this variable in URLs, as well. For example, you can send a user to a dashboard that shows a time range from six hours ago until now: `https://play.grafana.org/d/000000012/grafana-play-home?viewPanel=2&orgId=1?from=now-6h&to=now`",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__from` and `$__to`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72b5cea27c569545fe2d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use the `$__interval` variable as a parameter to group by time (for InfluxDB, MySQL, Postgres, MSSQL), Date histogram interval (for Elasticsearch), or as a _summarize_ function parameter (for Graphite).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f7e9b0408892fa7d44ac",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana automatically calculates an interval that can be used to group by time in queries. When there are more data points than can be shown on a graph, then queries can be made more efficient by grouping by a larger interval. It's more efficient to group by 1 day than by 10s when looking at 3 months of data. The graph looks the same and the query is faster. The `$__interval` is calculated using the time range and the width of the graph (the number of pixels).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4777bdbddeeffc09c871",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, when the time range is 1 hour and the graph is full screen, then the interval might be calculated to `2m` - points are grouped in 2 minute intervals. If the time range is 6 months and the graph is full screen, then the interval might be `1d` (1 day) - points are grouped by day.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 59,
        "lineEnd": 59,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L59-L59"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b75fc4b743a0c72c4f01",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the InfluxDB data source, the legacy variable `$interval` is the same variable. `$__interval` should be used instead.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a9a13bbf88a328675acc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The InfluxDB and Elasticsearch data sources have `Group by time interval` fields that are used to hard code the interval or to set the minimum limit for the `$__interval` variable (by using the `>` syntax -> `>10m`).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "47197c2d57632cafd89e881be4dbd3d8f67f4bca",
        "sha256": "96d599ac5546da4d5eff868adb4c39ebca5e8cd399dad64323c6d6aac90cab33",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f32d235e2edee13ee88c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This variable is the `$__interval` variable in milliseconds, not a time interval formatted string. For example, if the `$__interval` is `20m` then the `$__interval_ms` is `1200000`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Global variables",
        "`$__interval_ms`"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/dashboards/variables/global-variables.md",
