    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52de7431de10c6c43f96",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can apply the same steps to any data source. Correlations allow you to create links in visualizations to run dynamic queries based on selected data. In this example we used data returned by a query to build a new query generating different visualization using the same data source. However, you can create correlations between any data sources to create custom exploration flows.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Correlations Editor in Explore",
        "Correlations examples",
        "Create a text to graph correlation"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/correlations-editor-in-explore.md",
