    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c3b72037f7ecc0efa633",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also focus on this path by clicking the **Show critical path only** button in the **Span filters** options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Timeline"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 84,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L84-L84"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.97a7b5ed64428e8533f2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Traces are composed of one or more spans. A span is a unit of work within a trace that has a start time relative to the beginning of the trace, a duration and an operation name for the unit of work. It usually has a reference to a parent span, unless it’s the first span, the root span, in a trace. It frequently includes key/value attributes that are relevant to the span itself, for example the HTTP method used in the request, as well as other metadata such as the service name, sub-span events, or links to other spans.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 88,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L88-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff1619674788b7bf9b56",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can expand any span in a trace and view the details, including the span and resource attributes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c13342cedd209d032149",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Span details include span attributes, resource attributes, events, and links.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 97,
        "lineEnd": 97,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L97-L97"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.623a89186ad1e0e9bde5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Span attributes** are key-value pairs that provide metadata about a specific span. They give context to the operation being performed, such as information about the request, response, or any relevant operational details. For example, if the span deals with calling another service via HTTP, an attribute could include the HTTP URL (maybe as the span attribute key `http.url`) and the HTTP status code returned (as the span attribute `http.status_code`).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details",
        "Span and resource attributes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.efea5f8a0aa02c48bd90",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Events are log-like records attached to a span that represent an occurrence during its execution. They record notable moments or occurrences within the span's lifecycle, such as errors, warnings, or checkpoints. If an error occurs during an operation, an event can be added to the span to indicate what went wrong and when. Events include a timestamp, name, and key-value pairs attributes that provide additional context or details about the event.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details",
        "Events"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 113,
        "lineEnd": 113,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L113-L113"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.43b16ea4b8057ea2b80a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Links show relationships between spans that are not in a direct parent-child relationship. They represent associations between spans that happen concurrently or across separate trace trees, linking traces that originated from separate sources but are logically connected, such as background job processing initiated from a web request. You might use links when a trace passes through an asynchronous queue or when correlating traces from different services.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span details",
        "Links"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "dc5eb9f49e9ce6b27ad5fe937ee0dcf6ac6cea5f",
        "sha256": "028c8a575da3fe6cb4e8e5eb4e0b218296a3a433d13af79dd1299413e3f3bb1d",
        "lineStart": 119,
        "lineEnd": 119,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/explore/trace-integration.md#L119-L119"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.20b6aad1214730211927",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Span filters allow you to refine the spans displayed in the trace timeline viewer. The more filters you add, the more specific the filtered spans become. Click on a trace to access Span filters.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Traces in Explore",
        "Trace view",
        "Span filters"
      ],
      "source": {
