    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.65d8c31b9195e245e8d7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana supports the following value mapping types:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure value mappings",
        "Types of value mappings"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f5354caf63e5c2bce5ea20a50bf1bd77add9be7c",
        "sha256": "c5a2d32236e0b8527254f8a91c96546218016237cc9f33004475fc483cafa8b0",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b21b6659058bbaf04286",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A **Value** mapping maps specific values to text and a color. For example, you can configure a mapping so that all instances of the value `10` appear as **Perfection!** rather than the number. Use **Value** mapping when you want to format a single value. ![The value 10 mapped to the text Perfection!](/media/docs/grafana/panels-visualizations/screenshot-map-value-v10.4.png)",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure value mappings",
        "Types of value mappings",
        "Value"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f5354caf63e5c2bce5ea20a50bf1bd77add9be7c",
        "sha256": "c5a2d32236e0b8527254f8a91c96546218016237cc9f33004475fc483cafa8b0",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 135,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md#L134-L135"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f56b6d13693784d09c41",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A **Range** mapping maps numerical ranges to text and a color. For example, if a value is within a certain range, you can configure a range value mapping to display **Low** or **High** rather than the number. Use **Range** mapping when you want to format multiple, continuous values. ![Ranges of numbers mapped to the text Low and High with colors yellow and red](/media/docs/grafana/panels-visualizations/screenshot-map-range-v10.4.png)",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure value mappings",
        "Types of value mappings",
        "Range"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f5354caf63e5c2bce5ea20a50bf1bd77add9be7c",
        "sha256": "c5a2d32236e0b8527254f8a91c96546218016237cc9f33004475fc483cafa8b0",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 140,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md#L139-L140"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5fb97901c7172ca92c69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A **Regex** mapping maps regular expressions to text and a color. For example, if a value is `www.example.com`, you can configure a regular expression value mapping so that Grafana displays **www** and truncates the domain. Use the **Regex** mapping when you want to format the text and color of a regular expression value. ![A regular expression used to truncate full URLs to the text wwww](/media/docs/grafana/panels-visualizations/screenshot-map-regex-v10.4.png)",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure value mappings",
        "Types of value mappings",
        "Regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/configure-value-mappings/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f5354caf63e5c2bce5ea20a50bf1bd77add9be7c",
        "sha256": "c5a2d32236e0b8527254f8a91c96546218016237cc9f33004475fc483cafa8b0",
        "lineStart": 144,
        "lineEnd": 145,
