    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b615346d8dc31cfddbcd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Grafana Assistant](ref:assistant) brings AI-powered assistance to your SQL expressions workflow. Assistant knows SQL expressions, so it can explain a query, fix syntax errors, and suggest improvements using the correct MySQL-dialect syntax, table references, and column conventions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "SQL expressions",
        "Grafana Assistant integration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3e545e4b2f9dfa0e933cbe79b173d05a64036723",
        "sha256": "f821b02e2b87c25ad95fd5dee78a7973144d794c06fd2c6fcad576ccf23ed53d",
        "lineStart": 401,
        "lineEnd": 401,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md#L401-L401"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ad4c2466caf2ced14529",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also ask Assistant to build a panel using natural language. When you ask it to combine or correlate data across multiple queries, it prefers SQL expressions over join transformations and writes the SQL expression directly into your panel.",
      "headingPath": [
        "SQL expressions",
        "Grafana Assistant integration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3e545e4b2f9dfa0e933cbe79b173d05a64036723",
        "sha256": "f821b02e2b87c25ad95fd5dee78a7973144d794c06fd2c6fcad576ccf23ed53d",
        "lineStart": 403,
        "lineEnd": 403,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md#L403-L403"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bc9d60bc08c9a4798bd3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Assistant is generally available on Grafana Cloud and in public preview for Grafana OSS and Grafana Enterprise. On Grafana Enterprise (version 13.1 and later), Assistant comes pre-installed, so you only need to connect your Grafana Cloud account to start using it. On Grafana OSS, install the Assistant app from the plugin catalog and connect it to a Grafana Cloud stack. For more information, refer to the [Grafana Assistant documentation](ref:assistant).",
      "headingPath": [
        "SQL expressions",
        "Grafana Assistant integration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3e545e4b2f9dfa0e933cbe79b173d05a64036723",
        "sha256": "f821b02e2b87c25ad95fd5dee78a7973144d794c06fd2c6fcad576ccf23ed53d",
        "lineStart": 406,
        "lineEnd": 406,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md#L406-L406"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95022038ede480878655",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When Grafana Assistant is available on your instance, the SQL expression editor shows Assistant buttons to the right of the **Run query** button. When you use a button, Assistant opens in the sidebar with your SQL query, any query errors, and your schema column metadata already included as context, so it can reference the actual field names and types in your data. From there you get the full Assistant experience, including follow-up questions, conversation history, and access to the Assistant's built-in tools.",
      "headingPath": [
        "SQL expressions",
        "Grafana Assistant integration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/sql-expressions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3e545e4b2f9dfa0e933cbe79b173d05a64036723",
        "sha256": "f821b02e2b87c25ad95fd5dee78a7973144d794c06fd2c6fcad576ccf23ed53d",
        "lineStart": 409,
